-- title:
--   Original infinite-activity BV arbitrary-cofinal stopped marked noise plus supplied uniform-grid signed HJB B has integrable nonpositive expected sum at every physical row
-- statement:
--   Under the unchanged original spectrally negative Lévy bounded-variation dividend verification hypotheses with infinite negative mark activity, original true dividend control, and arbitrary prescribed spatial cofinal reserve bands, retain the exact uniform physical grid u, original compensated negative mark grid N from BVA60, and original signed discounted HJB physical generator B. Assume B is integrable and exactly defined by the original generator sum plus finite variation correction, with no change to the original driving Lévy path and mark measure. Prove for every physical row m that the literal sum N_m + B_m is integrable and its expected value is nonpositive. BVA60 supplies integrability and exact zero expectation of N_m for any prescribed bands; the Proved original p3_comp8 physical HJB theorem gives the integrable B mean sign; linearity completes the exact signed expectation ledger. This supplies the genuine source signed part used in BVA96 and A22, leaving the physical cash/contact positive L1 error as a separate obligation. The theorem retains actual infinite mark activity and does not choose a favourable spatial diagonal.

import Mathlib
